{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books","id":1073005,"title":"Let's hype the Dragon-Blooded and Realm books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-04T02:34:23-07:00","id":1073005,"title":"Let's hype the Dragon-Blooded and Realm books","content":"<b>My questions are as follows:</b><ul><li>What do you want to see in these books that you haven't really seen before?</li> <li>What do you want to make grand comebacks from previous editions?</li> <li>What don't you want to see in these books?</li> <li>What do you want to discuss or hype about these books?</li> </ul>Personally I would like to see depicted Gentes symbols just like we've had for the Great Houses. I never read any Dragon-Blood stuff from First Edition but I remember there being a lack of Lookshy related content in Second Edition. <br /> <br /> I want Roseblack to make a comeback. I've always been a Tepet Ejava fanboi waving flags and wearing &quot;Make the Realm great again&quot; caps. Give some Roseblack chapter fiction too.<br /> <br /> I don't want to see elemental surcharges. I don't want a constant reminder of the Dragon-Blooded being either antagonists or weak.<br /> <br /> I'm hyped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T02:53:13-07:00","id":1073010,"title":"","content":"This is my first edition of Exalted, so no idea about comebacks, but I am hoping to see info about Dragonblooded who aren't from the Realm or Lookshy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T03:08:47-07:00","id":1073011,"title":"","content":"I want the Great Houses and Lookshyan Gentes to absolutely <i>pop</i> with personality. I want them to be recognizably more than just &quot;the navy house, the orgy and drugs house, the military house, the other military house, the sneaky disgraced house&quot;, etc...<br /> <br /> Also a pronunciation guide for some of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T03:19:23-07:00","id":1073015,"title":"","content":"The mechanics are the big mystery to me when I was getting regular info the fluff was full of instances of 'wow, I didn't even know I wanted this and it's great!'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","user":"Bladewind","date":". 04-04-2017, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T03:29:52-07:00","id":1073016,"title":"","content":"Dragon blooded charms that are more elemental manipulation, and not dumbed-down and reskinned solar charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T03:36:06-07:00","id":1073021,"title":"","content":"My greatest hype is the book itself. The Dragon-Blooded have always been my favorites. I don't know why, they just resonate with me to a far greater degree than any other type of Exalted.<br /> <br /> I would love to get some ideas about the Dragon-Blooded beyond the Great Houses.<br /> - What about the early Dragon-Blooded who came to the Blessed Isle - where they all subsumed into the Great Houses, or are there Lesser Houses running around?<br /> - What about families of Dragon-Blooded not beholden to the Realm? There are the gentes in Lookshy, but any Dragon-Blood anywhere would understand the idea and power of building a family.<br /> <br /> I am very excited about the idea of multi-elemental Charms.<br /> I hope that elemental surcharges are gone, but if not, I will likely just house rule them away. I did it in 1st and 2nd edition, and can do so again.<br /> Finally, as Ekorren wrote, the reminders of Dragon-Blooded weakness do get a little annoying.<br /> <br /> I am certainly hyped too. It will be some time yet, but with the Deluxe Edition having literally just been given into my hands, today is a good day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T03:40:59-07:00","id":1073023,"title":"","content":"I'd like Cherak to get fleshed out, if they're going to be a wild card give them something to be a wild card.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T03:41:42-07:00","id":1073024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books?p=1073016#post1073016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon blooded charms that are more elemental manipulation, and not dumbed-down and reskinned solar charms</div> </div> </div> </div>There are more options than these two, and I want to see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T04:53:25-07:00","id":1073035,"title":"","content":"Lesser houses, outcasts, the gentes and cherak would be awesome. Some Shoganate era stuff would be great as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:01:29-07:00","id":1073039,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more attention given to the Lookshyan terrestrials, particularly Lookshy's immaculate order. It'd be cool if there were small differences in the Five Glorious Dragon Styles, differences that imply theological things that monks will fight over.<br /> <br /> I liked the idea of the Breeding prerequisite for charms in Dreams of the First Age, and I really liked the dynastic charms too. I'd like to see that come in, particularly the Presence charm that strengthens the blood of The Worthy. If not that, then something that explores the tragedy of the Dragons' gift being watered down and possibly some desperate &amp; costly way to combat it. Maybe even some group of Terrestrials lobbying (unsuccessfully) to restore the First Age prohibition against breeding with mortals.<br /> <br /> I'm real keen to see how the Immaculates interact with Mastery, and the Five Glorious Dragon Styles too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books?p=1073011#post1073011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a pronunciation guide for some of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeeeesssssssss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5716-thousand_comforts_base","name":"Thousand_Comforts_Base","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:33:36-07:00","id":1073051,"title":"","content":"I personally loved the bits about the various Realm academies but I want to some more in depth stuff on all of them given how important they are to a Dynast's upbringing.<br /> <br /> I would be excited to see some a more thorough understanding on how house hierarchies work and perhaps more pronounced differences in family dynamics and relationships amongst both the Gentes and Great Houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:35:11-07:00","id":1073054,"title":"","content":"Discussion of Prasad by way of groups of Dragon-Blooded who are not Lookshy or the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:44:23-07:00","id":1073055,"title":"","content":"<br /> What do you want to see in these books that you haven't really seen before?<br /> <br /> I know this isn't likely to happen, but I dream with a special Battlegroup system for Wyld Hunts. Cause you know, DB's are like the primary antagonists for solars and handling a complete Brotherhood is hard for a single individual.<br /> <br /> What do you want to make grand comebacks from previous editions?<br /> <br /> Immaculate Dragon Styles, I want monks to be freakin' awesome, I hope Fire Dragon has a way better version of the anima charm that did almost nothing in previous editions for example. And I need to see Wood Dragon now that it includes the use of staff!!!<br /> <br /> What don't you want to see in these books?<br /> <br /> Forest Witches... I don't get them nor care about them (at least in their previous presentation). All their background is like a Friday 13th movie. Very episodic in my opinion. Also I don't ever wanna see that stupid rock climbing craft charm again in my life.<br /> <br /> What do you want to discuss or hype about these books?<br /> <br /> Synergy between DB charms. Is it still a thing? Do people like that aspect of their mechanics? I know I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","user":"Gonzo","date":". 04-04-2017, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:46:01-07:00","id":1073056,"title":"","content":"I definitely want support for varied sorts of DBs (Dynasts, Lookshyans, Outcastes). I want fleshed-out Houses. I want cool Charms. Instead of &quot;solers r bettr, kek&quot; I want to see DBs being awesome and exciting, outweighing their relative weakness by having sides to their games you just don't really get with Solars.<br /> I want the Realm to feel alive and deep, grand and yet not unshitty.<br /> <br /> I want to get the same sense of &quot;oh SHIT this gives me like fifty character ideas&quot; that some homebrew projects have given me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T06:24:54-07:00","id":1073072,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-blooded have long been my favorite of the Exalted! Here's what I'm excited about<b></b>:<ul><li>Charm trees that aren't locked into a single element</li> <li>3rd edition look at the Blessed Isle</li> <li>More about the Realm in the threshold with more information about the satrapies</li> <li>3rd edition take on Lookshy and other non-Dynast Dragon-blooded</li> <li>The promise of Great Houses with stronger identity</li> <li>Everything else :-)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:08:02-07:00","id":1073096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books?p=1073055#post1073055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forest Witches... I don't get them nor care about them (at least in their previous presentation). All their background is like a Friday 13th movie. Very episodic in my opinion. Also I don't ever wanna see that stupid rock climbing craft charm again in my life.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, I desperately want more about the Forest Witches. To each their own, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:25:12-07:00","id":1073177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books#post1073005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My questions are as follows:</b><ul><li>What do you want to see in these books that you haven't really seen before?</li> <li>What do you want to make grand comebacks from previous editions?</li> <li>What don't you want to see in these books?</li> <li>What do you want to discuss or hype about these books?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I want to see a Western enclave of non-Realm Dragon-Blooded that's more numerous than 2. Eos and Ossissa are great, but they're no society! Marahd is so lonely! The Caul is great, but that's a Realm thing (at least mostly?). The North has Cherak (which can be played as very apart from the Realm), the East has Lookshy and the Forest Witches, and the South has the Pure Way in Prasad now. This could be a good middle ground between 'no more Forest Witches' and 'tell me everything about Forest Witches'. <br /> I want to see Lesser Houses - work up to the Great Houses!<br /> I want to see Shogunate glory thrown about all over the place - &quot;This has been my family's ancestral home since before the Scarlet Empress. I don't care what paper you managed to have Tepet Fokuf sign, you won't move me from my Manse without a fight!&quot; &quot;I am the last Shogun's true blood. My claim to the Dragon Throne is at least as true as the late Empress' children.&quot; &quot;Now that the Empress is gone, our ambition can soar like it once did in the Shogunate. Together, sister, we will carve our names across Creation and no one will stop us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Comebacks - totally want the Five Dragon Styles, but I'll be completely surprised if we don't get those. I want the deadly decadent empire. <br /> <br /> Please no - short Charm trees. They're Ability based (Specialty based?) Exalted, so they should have some nice deep Charm trees to differentiate themselves.<br /> <br /> HYPE - This is Exalted content! I am already completely hype!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:33:22-07:00","id":1073184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books#post1073005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My questions are as follows:</b><ul><li>Q1) What do you want to see in these books that you haven't really seen before?</li> <li>Q2) What do you want to make grand comebacks from previous editions?</li> <li>Q3) What don't you want to see in these books?</li> <li>Q4) What do you want to discuss or hype about these books?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Good questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1) I'd like to see some solid Patrician details (Isle and Threshold based). I'd be very happy if 3 families were named in each of the DB book's House write ups, even if it was just a single line. Then the Patrician families could have expanded details in the Realm book. Plot hooks would be nice, but 'how' the Patricians conduct business and seek to attract/hold favor with the Great Houses is something worthy of exploration. Are they just as cut throat as the Houses? Do they meddle in Threshold affairs? And what sort of influence can they bring to bear? In essence, they need to be more like the colorful Banner Houses from a Song of Ice and Fire (IMO) than the wealthy wallflowers from previous editions.<br /> <br /> 2) Fun/useful stuff like the Palace of Tamed Storms, an 'updated for 3e' version of 2e's Chapter 7 Storytelling, and NPCs like the villainous Peleps Deled to stir things up.<br /> <br /> 3) I don't want to see 700+ years of Realm history boil down to 'anything of minor consequence or greater... was <b>only</b> done by the Empress'. Let the Patricians and Great Houses have some historic mentions too, her Redness can surely delegate a few things (or just eat popcorn &amp; watch) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Also I don't want to see the following topic ignored: How 700+ years of sorcery/workings/Heptagram influence has changed or improved the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Long time lurker","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8781-happy-hermit","name":"Happy Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8781_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:41:41-07:00","id":1073196,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>I'd like to see collaborative effects when multiple DB's use the same charm (or different charms that enhance each other). I don't think every charm needs this effect, but a solid enough portion of them that it's &quot;a thing&quot;.</li> <li>I see this as an opportunity to revamp collaboration rules for working together on things, something that is scarcely touched upon in the core book. I want to see 2 DB's fighting together to be <b>more </b>than twice as bad as 1 DB. Not only are there 2 of them, but they cover, bolster, and enhance each other.</li> <li>I want to be able to tell the Great Houses apart at a glance. While I'd love to have multiple pages on each House to dive into, I'd like a single paragraph to show me how 2 houses with Military focus can be discernibly different so that it's meaningful to PCs that encounter those houses.</li> <li>I could use more examples of Battlegroups that comprise Realm and Lookshyian soldiers for DBs to command. Archer groups, cavalry, siege, etc.</li> <li>It has been hinted that The Blessed Isle is &quot;Creation in miniature&quot; where it's colder in the north side of the island, and hotter on the south side, and not just &quot;temperate throughout&quot;. I'd like to see this maintained and used in examples of different places all over the Isle so people are reminded of it. For example, if the Heptagram is still in the north part of the island, it should deal with snow and ice during some parts of the year at least.</li> <li>I'd like to see a fresh perspective on The Immaculate Order. I have no thoughts on how to do this myself, but something that brings new insight to the order that's not just a rehash of the past 2 editions. This could be excerpts from The Doctrine, to more examples of how the Order does it's duties both on the Blessed Isle and across Creation.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:45:02-07:00","id":1073199,"title":"","content":"I think it's probably a bit early to be hyping DBs, Arms is a couple months out yet and DBs is probably going to be a December release or something. I'm not even complaining there's just that much work to do.<br /> <br /> That being saaaiiid, I'm still so frekin' hype. I'm excited to see how their charm frees will work without supernals, I want to really feel the differences between the houses. <br /> <br /> Mostly though I'm just looking forward to playing. I haven't played a DB in forever, like five years or more. I'm really looking forwards to the backgrounds stuff, solars get ten points now so maybe DBs will get like fifteen or something, or some of the two for one ones. <br /> <br /> I'm also really looking forward to some weaker exalts who can have a decent fight against more of the antagonists chapter, which should be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:28:13-07:00","id":1073233,"title":"","content":"Lesser Houses. How do they compete with the Great Houses economically and politically? How involved are they with the satrapies? What opportunities do they have for expansion? What lengths are they willing to go to in order to improve their situation? How are the lesser Houses founded? How would you go about founding a Lesser House while the Empress is gone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:33:41-07:00","id":1073237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books?p=1073055#post1073055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this isn't likely to happen, but I dream with a special Battlegroup system for Wyld Hunts. Cause you know, DB's are like the primary antagonists for solars and handling a complete Brotherhood is hard for a single individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Wyld Hunt needs a separate subsystem/modification of the Battlegroup rules, but a section on Wyld Hunt tactics and storytelling the Hunt, either in Dragon-Blooded, Realm or Vance's proposed Storyteller Guide (or as, like, a blog post that eventually goes in the ST Guide) would be welcome. <br /> <br /> I'd like to see the Wyld Hunt treated from the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded in their own book, presented in a way that makes it easier to show them as neither evil nor dupes of a fake religion. The early chapters of God-Kicking Boot come to mind -- from the perspective of <i>everyone in that scene</i>, the Dragon-Blooded Satrap throwing down with the Lunar was pretty much the good guy. And, of course, the Solars and Lunars are so few and far between that, even with a special religious duty to prioritize those targets, the Wyld Hunt probably spends most of its time fighting Fair Folk, the dead, and rogue spirits.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely like to see some more in-depth presentation on the Lookshyan Gentes, the Realm's minor houses, and Dragon-Blooded from the rest of Creation.<br /> <br /> I'd very much like a pretty in-depth treatment of the struggle for the throne in the Realm book -- give the Roseblack some time to shine because she's awesome, give us some more substance on some of the dark-horse candidates, maybe point out what some of the pillars of each House's current position are, to give players and STs some idea of where to go when they want to shake things up.<br /> <br /> Considering how heavily bureaucratic the Realm is, I'd hope we'd get some more fleshing-out of the Bureaucracy ability; I doubt they'll do up a whole Bureaucracy subsystem, and considering how obnoxious subsystem proliferation can get I'm not sure I'd want them to, but some more examples and guidelines would be welcome. The Project rules as they exist in the corebook don't exactly pop, at least in my opinion.<br /> <br /> A little bit more information on the Shogunate would be nice -- enough to spark some imaginations, but leave most of it undefined. I think we're kind of getting into that with Arms, though -- the Era tags inherently make some part of the Artifact lore into Shogunate lore, and I think telling the stories of the Shogunate and the First Age through the wonders they left behind is very much in-theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7058-kerredai","name":"Kerredai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:45:40-07:00","id":1073245,"title":"","content":"The one thing I would like to see is minor Houses. Especially Houses that don't have major blood ties to the Empress. <br /> <br /> One thing that often gets overlooked is that after Empress secured the Realm, there were already many Dragon Blooded families living there, and many other Dragon Blooded traveled from the Threshold to live in the Realm. <br /> <br /> There really should be families of Dragon Blooded who don't descend from the Empress and instead trace their lineage back to the Shogunate or even earlier. Now, the Realm is highly nepotistic, so families that don't trace their descent to the Empress would find themselves somewhat limited and obstructed, but I think some of those families should absolutely be considered minor Houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T18:14:35-07:00","id":1073479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerredai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books?p=1073237#post1073237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see the Wyld Hunt treated from the perspective of the Dragon-Blooded in their own book, presented in a way that makes it easier to show them as neither evil nor dupes of a fake religion. The early chapters of God-Kicking Boot come to mind -- from the perspective of <i>everyone in that scene</i>, the Dragon-Blooded Satrap throwing down with the Lunar was pretty much the good guy. And, of course, the Solars and Lunars are so few and far between that, even with a special religious duty to prioritize those targets, the Wyld Hunt probably spends most of its time fighting Fair Folk, the dead, and rogue spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, indeed, and I'd like it to be remembered that a Wyld Hunt is now not something specific to the great powers, but a banner under which Dragonblooded from <i>anywhere</i> put aside differences to tackle whatever they deem Anathema. Some expansion on that idea would be nice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T15:16:01-07:00","id":1073900,"title":"","content":"I'm a huge strategy game nerd, so I'm pretty stoked for the extra War material (sample strategems, etc.) that's likely to come alongside the discussion of the legions and the DB War charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11796-sergregness","name":"serGregness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11796_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T15:49:34-07:00","id":1073911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1073005-let-s-hype-the-dragon-blooded-and-realm-books?p=1073479#post1073479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, indeed, and I'd like it to be remembered that a Wyld Hunt is now not something specific to the great powers, but a banner under which Dragonblooded from <i>anywhere</i> put aside differences to tackle whatever they deem Anathema. Some expansion on that idea would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seven Arrows is a Wood Aspect who rules the Kingdom of Diamond Sand in the far South. Along its eastern boarder runs the Darakhal Sultanate, an ancient city-state with a hereditary mortal king. Their general is called Ashen Breeze, a Fire Aspect who has spent much of her life protecting the Sultanate. Ashen Breeze and Seven Arrows despise one another, and the Kingdom of Diamond Sand and the Darakhal Sultanate have been in a state of war for the last century.<br /> <br /> One day, Seven Arrows receives word that a Solar Exalted has appeared in the wastelands two hundred miles south of his kingdom. He sends a message to Ashen Breeze, proposing a temporary truce between his nation and the Sultanate (the first one since war broke out 95 years ago), that the two of them might fight against the Solar. Ashen Breeze loathes Seven Arrows, but recognizes that the Solar Anathema represents a far more dangerous threat, and so she agrees.<br /> <br /> The two of them send out messages to the other nearby Dragon Blooded that they can. One message is sent to the Dragon Blooded simply known as Sapphire, who lives several hundred miles to the west, deep within the desert. She is an ancient sorceress who has been studying her magic longer than anyone can remember. Another goes to Silver Eyes, a young Dragon Blooded merchant with a big ego who has been causing problems with the Guild. Neither Seven Arrows nor Ashen Breeze like him, but he is a Dragon Blooded all the same. The final message is sent to Ledaal Tesriss, a Realm Dragon Blooded who arrived in the area a few months earlier to excavate and explore an old Shogunate ruin.<br /> <br /> The five of them soon gather together. They hold wildly different beliefs and come from different lands. Some of them outright despise one another. But the one thing they have in common is that they share the Blood of the Dragons, and each one recognizes that they are the first and last line of defense that Creation has to protect itself from the Anathema that would threaten it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I can't wait to run some games with this as the premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-05-2017, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T00:33:58-07:00","id":1074043,"title":"","content":"I want (a) working cooperation mechanic(s). The Cooperative keyword never did anything worthwhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T01:42:54-07:00","id":1074056,"title":"","content":"I'd like the great Houses to not be flanderised. That's the only thing I'm actually worried about, since people keep saying &quot;the houses are too similar, make them really different&quot; (which I don't agree with, but there you go), so I'm a little worried that the Houses will become un-nuanced Houses of Hats (this is the spy house! This is the fundamentalist house! etc). But I think the fluff writers are good enough that it should be okay.<br /> So, yes, nuance.<br /> <br /> I'd like the Realm to have more of a sense of history. How did it develop? What happened to the 12 houses that no longer exist? What happened to all the Shogunate-era gents who were absorbed by the Realm? Often the history makes it seem like random DBs with no ties or backstory whatsoever appeared, screwed the Empress, and bam, great house.<br /> <br /> I'd also like the dates to make more sense!<br /> <br /> Mechanically, not much to say, as what I've heard sounds good. Surcharges out, charms that don't work against celestials out. I'd like the charms to have a more even power level so you don't get every DB group having the same collection of charms, but that should happen automatically.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind better co-operative charms; they were rubbish in 2nd ed so hardly ever got used. Except when you wanted to blow up a warstrider or magitech airship or something.<br /> <br /> I'd like a few more examples of non-Realm DB families.<br /> I'd like a few more examples of minor houses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-06-2017, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T01:43:17-07:00","id":1074057,"title":"","content":"The thing I would like to see a LOT of in this book is to make the dragon-blooded be &quot;the heroes&quot; of their book.<br /> <br /> No more cases of &quot;that anathema who just exalted went ahead and killed these fifteen elders and took a dump in mnemons cornflakes and got away with it&quot;.<br /> <br /> More of the supposed &quot;cooperation&quot; power that dragon-blooded posses. Give me elemental &quot;combos&quot; where the power of one aspect can trigger a new effect if a different aspect does something and things like that.<br /> <br /> More of the everyday life of the dragon-blooded, heck for me I would love to know more about what's considered a delicacy, what style of clothes is common, what is the &quot;social code&quot; of each house/gentes.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded kicking all kinds of butts!<br /> <br /> Some more places where there are &quot;gatherings&quot; of dragon-blooded other than the realm, lookshy and that new place...<br /> <br /> Possibly a guide to making your own lesser house/gentes? Possibly similar to what they have in the song of ice and fire rpg.<br /> <br /> I DO NOT want to hear a singel word about how solars or any other exalt is oh so superior to the weak little rank and files that are the dragon-blooded! It's the dragon-blooded's book so they should be the strongest in their book and they should be the ones winning!<br /> <br /> I don't want to see any of that silly &quot;this costs extra cause screw you&quot; thing...<br /> <br /> Immaculate styles. GIMME GIMME GIMME!<br /> <br /> The legions, give us some famous units or straight up legions, let the story tellers watch with glee as their players squirm as they hear the name of some famous legion and that it's heading their way!<br /> More details in general for the legions would be nice, possibly some new neat mass combat additions (mass combat tags?).<br /> <br /> Give us some dragon-blooded NEWLY created wonders. They are gods damned exalts they should be making cool stuff!<br /> <br /> Give us some fancy examples of social intrigues!<br /> <br /> I hope I made some sense!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T02:30:18-07:00","id":1074064,"title":"","content":"At the very least, dragonblooded should play David to the solar's Goliath.<br /> <br /> Tales where they stood united against the admittedly-superior might of the anathema and emerged victorious nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T05:16:16-07:00","id":1074095,"title":"","content":"Unless you're approaching David and Goliath as stand ins for their nations, the actual David person is pretty darn Solaristic to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T14:29:07-07:00","id":1074317,"title":"","content":"Well, yes, but this is always the dichotomy of the Solars+Dragonblood relationship. Both can be seen as the Davids from one perspective, both can be seen as the Goliaths from the other perspective.<br /> <br /> Also, doesn't Exalted now have a place called Goliath in the South? I'm sure I remember something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}